  "paraphrase": "For every grid function grid(n, k, i, j) defined as i.succ + j.succ - k, and for every valid predicate valid(n, k) defined by the conditions 0 < n, 0 < k, and the existence of an injective function f such that the range of grid(n, k, i, f(i)) equals the interval [1, n), it follows that the set of all pairs (n, k) for which valid(n, k) holds is equal to putnam_2024_b1_solution."
